# The framework trial as a COS pipeline — James, 2026-11-13: "we have ollama now. lets leverage that. test, benchmark, run the trial in the docs
# folder. clearglass pipelines, raid pipelines, idearium, all of them in cos." The trial (docs/framework-trial): six problems, each asked with and
# without his method, judged blind. Each step calls the trial's own screen (docs/framework-trial/server.js, :4820); it runs trial.js, which asks
# Ollama directly. One problem per step (a request waits at most about 5 min). Judging stays his and blind: the run holds at "judged" until the
# screen has scores, and goes on when he presses Continue. Nothing here is new code: api steps on the routes the screen already serves.
envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-pipeline-framework-trial
type: pipeline
id: framework-trial
context: COS › pipelines (shipped with COS; run by COS's engine)
intent: >-
  The framework trial, run by Ollama: each of six problems asked with and without his method (arms A and B), the answers blinded, his blind
  scores waited for, then arm B scored against arm A, and the benchmark per model.
summary: 11 tasks · the trial's own routes · Ollama
system: cos
tags:
  - pipeline
  - trial
  - ollama
  - bundled
source: cos/pipeline/pipelines
occurrences: 1
payload:
  id: framework-trial
  format: nexus-pipeline
  version: 1
  name: Framework trial (Ollama)
  description: >-
    The framework trial (docs/framework-trial), run by Ollama: P1-P6 each asked with arm A (baseline) and arm B (his method), blinded, his
    blind scores waited for, then arm B scored against arm A, and the benchmark (time, tokens, tokens per second) per model. Start the trial's
    screen first: node docs/framework-trial/server.js. Set vars.model to an installed Ollama model (ollama:<name>), vars.run to a run number.
  vars:
    model: ollama:qwen2.5-coder:7b   # an installed Ollama model, written ollama:<name>
    run: 1                           # the run number: answers/<P>/<model>-<arm>-<run>.md; a second run gives the same cells a second sample
    port: 4820                       # the trial's screen (TRIAL_UI_PORT)
  settings:
    parallel: 1
  tasks:
    - id: screen
      label: The trial's screen answers
      depends_on: []
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: http://127.0.0.1:{{vars.port}}/api/state
          method: GET
          timeoutMs: 10000
      gate:
        contains: '"problems"'
      retries: 2
      onFail: hold   # not up: start it (node docs/framework-trial/server.js), then Continue
    - id: p1
      label: P1, both arms, by {{vars.model}}
      depends_on:
        - screen
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: http://127.0.0.1:{{vars.port}}/api/deploy
          method: POST
          body: '{"models":["{{vars.model}}"],"arm":"both","run":{{vars.run}},"problem":"P1"}'
          timeoutMs: 290000   # one problem, two answers: under the ~5 min a request can wait
      gate:
        matches: '"ok":true[\s\S]*deployed 2 answer'
      retries: 1
    - id: p2
      label: P2, both arms, by {{vars.model}}
      depends_on:
        - p1
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: http://127.0.0.1:{{vars.port}}/api/deploy
          method: POST
          body: '{"models":["{{vars.model}}"],"arm":"both","run":{{vars.run}},"problem":"P2"}'
          timeoutMs: 290000   # one problem, two answers: under the ~5 min a request can wait
      gate:
        matches: '"ok":true[\s\S]*deployed 2 answer'
      retries: 1
    - id: p3
      label: P3, both arms, by {{vars.model}}
      depends_on:
        - p2
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: http://127.0.0.1:{{vars.port}}/api/deploy
          method: POST
          body: '{"models":["{{vars.model}}"],"arm":"both","run":{{vars.run}},"problem":"P3"}'
          timeoutMs: 290000   # one problem, two answers: under the ~5 min a request can wait
      gate:
        matches: '"ok":true[\s\S]*deployed 2 answer'
      retries: 1
    - id: p4
      label: P4, both arms, by {{vars.model}}
      depends_on:
        - p3
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: http://127.0.0.1:{{vars.port}}/api/deploy
          method: POST
          body: '{"models":["{{vars.model}}"],"arm":"both","run":{{vars.run}},"problem":"P4"}'
          timeoutMs: 290000   # one problem, two answers: under the ~5 min a request can wait
      gate:
        matches: '"ok":true[\s\S]*deployed 2 answer'
      retries: 1
    - id: p5
      label: P5, both arms, by {{vars.model}}
      depends_on:
        - p4
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: http://127.0.0.1:{{vars.port}}/api/deploy
          method: POST
          body: '{"models":["{{vars.model}}"],"arm":"both","run":{{vars.run}},"problem":"P5"}'
          timeoutMs: 290000   # one problem, two answers: under the ~5 min a request can wait
      gate:
        matches: '"ok":true[\s\S]*deployed 2 answer'
      retries: 1
    - id: p6
      label: P6, both arms, by {{vars.model}}
      depends_on:
        - p5
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: http://127.0.0.1:{{vars.port}}/api/deploy
          method: POST
          body: '{"models":["{{vars.model}}"],"arm":"both","run":{{vars.run}},"problem":"P6"}'
          timeoutMs: 290000   # one problem, two answers: under the ~5 min a request can wait
      gate:
        matches: '"ok":true[\s\S]*deployed 2 answer'
      retries: 1
    - id: blind
      label: Blind the answers (the key stays closed)
      depends_on:
        - p6
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: http://127.0.0.1:{{vars.port}}/api/blind
          method: POST
          body: '{}'
          timeoutMs: 60000
      gate:
        contains: '"ok":true'
    - id: judged
      label: Waits for your scores (the trial's screen, blind)
      depends_on:
        - blind
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: http://127.0.0.1:{{vars.port}}/api/state
          method: GET
      gate:
        matches: '"scored":[1-9]'
      onFail: hold   # judging is his, blind: score on the trial's screen (http://127.0.0.1:4820), then Continue
    - id: score
      label: Score, arm B against arm A
      depends_on:
        - judged
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: http://127.0.0.1:{{vars.port}}/api/score
          method: POST
          body: '{}'
          timeoutMs: 60000
      gate:
        contains: '"ok":true'
    - id: bench
      label: The benchmark, per model
      depends_on:
        - score
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: http://127.0.0.1:{{vars.port}}/api/state
          method: GET
      gate:
        contains: '"bench"' 
